# cuts/v1.0.37/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.37. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.37 and by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh.
#
# WHY v1.0.37 EXISTS: THE DEDUPE BUTTONS HAVE NEVER SAVED A DECISION, ONCE.
#
# Andy has reported "Could not save" on the duplicate-review controls at least
# a dozen times. Measured on his live box on 2026-08-19, the Doctor's log holds
# exactly ONE POST to /api/v1/wiki/duplicates/decision across its ENTIRE
# history, and that one was a diagnostic probe sent by an agent.
# ~/.ostler/corrections/duplicates.yaml does not exist. Not "sometimes fails":
# never once succeeded.
#
# MECHANISM. dup_decision.js decided whether a decision could be sent by
# reading location.hostname and treating a loopback value as proof of being on
# the Hub Mac. A loopback hostname is not evidence about the Hub. It is
# evidence about the VIEWER. An `ssh -L 8044:localhost:8044` forward, a
# container port map, or any local proxy all satisfy it on a machine that has
# no Doctor on it, so the controls stayed LIVE precisely where they could not
# work. The same predicate read a legitimate reverse proxy on a real hostname
# as remote and hid controls that WOULD have worked. One inference, wrong in
# both directions.
#
# The disable-off-Hub work (CM044 d92dbed, 2026-07-27) was right in intent.
# Its detector was the defect. It now probes /doctor/api/health on load.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALSO IN THIS CUT
#
#   CM051 #871  the operator-PII scan no longer depends on apt for ripgrep.
#               apt stalled 33 minutes on a mirror on 2026-08-18 and the
#               5-minute bound added in response converted one hang into two
#               timeouts the next day, blocking the one enforced cut RED both
#               times. A timeout makes an outage faster, not rarer.
#   CM051 #870  TNM's vendor/doctor graft. This WAS the one enforced cut RED.
#   CM051 #873  the wiki re-pin below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PINS BELOW ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
